    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298-a4">

                <pb facs="0787" n="665" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg665"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No.
                    27.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. Bea, Bellido &amp; Co., to Mr.
                    Pierce.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Matanzas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-09-11"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 11,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>We have the honor to inclose to you herewith two communications received from the
                    principal administration of customs, referring to a fine imposed on the captain
                    of the American steam-ship <hi rendition="#italic">Manhattan</hi> for
                    non-delivery of packages. As it demands of us payment by judicial procedure, we
                    refer the matter to you, that you may notify the said captain.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bea, Bellido</hi> &amp; Co.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
